  "comments": "Place in eastern gTsang in the area of sKyeg in Nyang stod, south of rGyal rtse (ID:6454). \r\nThe gNas rning temple was founded by rGya 'Jam dpal gsang ba (ca. 760-859) under the patronage of the mGos clan ([4LDAV8UH]: 82 and 86). It remained structurally unchanged from the 9th c. to 1045, when it became a bKa' gdams pa center ([4LDAV8UH]: 90)\r\nFor the history of the lineages, see [4LDAV8UH].\r\nMonasteries composing the gNas rnying stong skor after the Hor invasion are listed in [Y2ZN5C6X] (cited in [4LDAV8UH]: 103): \"dge ba bshes gnyen Kan logs pa, Rgya ston pa, Zla ba, Ston shag, Zla grags kyi dben pa, Gyan sa pa, Ye shes dpal, Rin 'od, Ston nam, Chos sgrub, and Sher 'bum. Moreover, Men rgan pa, Ser 'phreng pa, La drug pa, Byang mo khung pa, Drug ma ba, Lha khang pa, Mkhar ra lung pa, Grags shongs pa, Dge sdings pa, Dgon khra, 'Phang thang, Phro sdings, Sypi bsdus, Ser sdings, Dga' ldan, Dben tsha, Grum chung, G.ya' dmar ra, Rkyang po, Chu bzang, 'Bras mo, She mgur, Wa lung, Grog ra, Rmog pa, Ze thang, 'Chad mangs, Byangs mang, Bra than, Bye mda', Rtsid Gnas rnying, Nyan tsho, Stag lung, and Lho Dol.\"",
